<decision #track.execute-ai-data-workflow-through-eidolon-runtime.driver-boundary { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" }
(
  <question ?>Which layer owns mutable DAG semantics and which layer drives effects?</?>
  <answer { } (
    <raw-answer ?>depa-flows owns RunGraph semantics; Eidolon owns host application and effect authorities.</?>
    <decision-text ?>Use canonical graph/patch/invalidation/reuse functions and add only a persisted Eidolon driver over their ready frontier.</?>
    <rationale ?>This preserves product semantics without introducing a parallel workflow core.</?>
  )>
)>
